commit 521faee78789713311b9ad3fd0e52ab920385c6f
Author: Ahmet Egesel <ahmet.egesel@albil.com.tr>
Date:   Mon Sep 21 15:09:27 2026 +0300

    docs(corpus): reconcile seven repositories against their real drift windows
    
    The windows were measured from each clone's own pre-fetch HEAD, not from
    a date: the previous reconciliation ran against checkouts that were
    already nine days stale, which understated every window by roughly 3x
    (V3 read 5 files where 36 were real; ReactRouter 120 where 309 were).
    
    Piri.Pho.V3 (36 files): search sorting is opt-in, so the doc's "defaults
    to publish date" was false; cache telemetry, the reference map and its
    tripwire; one fixed pitfall retired.
    
    piri-pho-graphql (40): sport data now reads from Piri.Pho.V3's REST API
    for the internal app only - a moved repository boundary. The count cap
    means two different things on Mongo and Elasticsearch, so reading it as
    a performance control is right for a list and wrong for a search.
    
    Piri.Pho.Jurnal (47) plus a new unit, seo-metadata-management: the SEO
    module shares three letters with seo-content-catalog and nothing else -
    different domain object, zero mechanism overlap, and the catalog's own
    member regex structurally cannot match it.
    
    Piri.Yenisafak.UI.Nuxt: no window at all. Its code has not moved since
    before the corpus baseline, so this is a verification pass; two claims
    were wrong as written and corrected.
    
    Piri.Yenisafak.UI.ReactRouter (309): identity calls left the component
    package entirely and became props, now lint-enforced; the corpus said
    React Router v7 at five sites while the code runs v8.
    
    Piri.TVNET.Astro (679, one idea): packages/ui became a base skeleton and
    the brands carry the look. The standing claim that a missing brand key
    "retains the base skeleton look" was backwards - base emits ~800 classes
    it defines nowhere, so a decline renders unstyled, not skeletal.
    
    piriAppWebviewFlutter: already current.
    
    Also: 20 cross-references added where a doc pinned its own invariant to a
    neighbour's file - widening those globs would dissolve the unit
    boundaries, so the fix is navigational. Corpus-wide, 1430 refs now
    resolve with none dead.

