-  sources: [src/layouts/**, src/templates/**, src/components/layout/**, src/components/AppHeader.vue, src/components/AppSidebar.vue, src/components/AppSidebarBackup.vue, src/components/PhoBreadcrumbs.vue, src/components/index.js, src/components/constants.js, src/components/add-content/**, src/components/editors-handbook/**]
+  sources: [src/layouts/**, src/templates/**, src/components/layout/**, src/components/AppHeader.vue, src/components/AppSidebar.vue, src/components/AppSidebarBackup.vue, src/components/PhoBreadcrumbs.vue, src/components/index.js, src/components/constants.js, src/components/add-content/**, src/components/editors-handbook/**, src/modules/settings/menu/useMenu.js]
   keywords: [app shell, sayfa iskeleti, üst menü, yan menü, nav rail, mini-variant drawer, hamburger menu, responsive sidebar, sticky sidebar, layout picker, shell wrapper, ekmek kırıntısı, kullanıcı menüsü, marka değiştirici, eski sidebar, yetkisiz erişim sayfası, sayfa bulunamadı, dark mode toggle, collapse to dialog, vuetify application bar]
 
 @responsibilities
   - "Select which shell wraps a route: Base (full chrome), Default (bare card), SideMenu (side-nav plus content), Empty (no chrome), or Error (dialog for failures)."
   - "Host the persistent app-wide header and icon-rail sidebar inside Base, so every route gets the same top bar and site-switcher regardless of its section layout."
-  - "Build and filter the per-section side navigation from the route tree, respecting visibility flags, then hand off to a shared presentational menu-list component."
+  - "Build and filter the per-section side navigation from the route tree through the shared menu builder, applying the show-in-menu, permission and role gates, then hand off to a shared presentational menu-list component."
   - "Own the imperative global dialog handles wired onto the app root from inside Base so any descendant can trigger a confirm/alert/toast without prop drilling."
   - "Render route-derived breadcrumbs inside the header, keyed off the matched route chain."
   - "Collapse the persistent side-menu column into a floating-button-triggered dialog on small viewports."
@@ -52,6 +52,14 @@
     evidence: "AddContent.vue (contentTypeRoutes)"
     detail ::
       It wraps the content-type routes in a synthetic menu parent with the show-in-menu flag forced on, runs them through the shared menu builder so permission and visibility filtering apply, and renders one icon per surviving route. Adding a content-type route therefore adds its icon here without a further edit.
+  - rule: "The shared menu builder lives under the site-menu settings module despite belonging to this unit."
+    evidence: "useMenu.js (mapChildren, isVisible); AppSidebar.vue (useMenu); SideMenu.vue (useMenu); SideMenuContainer.vue (useMenu); AddContent.vue (useMenu)"
+    detail ::
+      src/modules/settings/menu/useMenu.js is the ONE builder every nav surface here imports - the icon rail, the section side menu, its collapsed container, and the header quick-add strip. Its directory belongs to the public-site menu editor capability and its name collides with that capability's vocabulary, but nothing in that capability imports it; it is this unit's code sitting in the wrong folder (see site-menu-builder.md#pitfalls). It is named in this unit's sources for that reason.
+  - rule: "A menu entry is visible only when its permission AND its role gate both pass."
+    evidence: "useMenu.js (isVisible, hasRequiredRole, isActive)"
+    detail ::
+      The builder composes two independent checks per entry. The permission check treats an absent meta.permission as visible and otherwise requires the grant on the active site. The role check treats an absent meta.roles as visible and otherwise requires the user to hold one of the listed role ids, compared as strings. Both apply at group level and at leaf level, and a group whose children all fail is dropped rather than rendered empty. The role half deliberately mirrors the router guard's own gate (see routing-and-access-control.md#contract) - they are two separate implementations of one rule, and a route gated in one place but not the other either offers a page that bounces or hides a page the user may open.
   - rule: "The editors' handbook is a non-dismissable dialog whose acceptance is remembered per browser, not per user."
     evidence: "EditorsHandbook.vue (editorsHandbookAcceptedKey)"
     detail ::
